Monitoring, evaluation, and reporting mechanisms to track progress and ensure accountability.
International cooperation and knowledge exchange within the Francophonie.
The document highlights participatory governance, policy coherence, and the need for long-term sustainability planning as core elements for SNDD success.', 'This document serves as a practical guide for the development of National Strategies for Sustainable Development (SNDD) within Francophone countries. It builds on international commitments from the Rio (1992) and Johannesburg (2002) Summits and aligns with the principles of Agenda 21. The guide aims to provide a structured methodology for governments to design and implement sustainable development strategies.

