The guidelines aim to strengthen investor confidence in Green Bonds, align Morocco with international climate finance standards, and mobilize capital for sustainable projects.', 'Morocco', 'climate', 'in_force', '2017-01-01'::date, 'Morocco', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/122_3', ARRAY['guidance_frameworks', 'sdg13', 'other sustainability policy', 'sdg7', 'sdg11', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'sdg9', 'voluntary', 'morocco']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('d812a5bb-f86b-5117-aeb9-226ab2aae67a', 'Morocco National Charter for Environment and Sustainable Development', 'Law No. 99-12 Establishing the National Charter for Environment and Sustainable Development', 'The Loi-cadre n° 99-12, promulgated in 2014, establishes Morocco’s national framework for environmental protection and sustainable development. It defines fundamental principles, objectives, and governance mechanisms for integrating sustainability into national policies. The law aims to:

Enhance environmental protection, biodiversity conservation, and pollution prevention.
Integrate sustainable development into sectoral policies and adopt a national strategy.
Align national legal frameworks with international environmental conventions.
Strengthen climate change adaptation and desertification control measures.
Establish environmental governance through institutional, economic, and financial reforms.
Define responsibilities of the state, local authorities, public institutions, private enterprises, and civil society.
Introduce environmental liability and control mechanisms, including environmental police and fiscal measures.
The law mandates territorial, social, and intergenerational solidarity principles and promotes public participation, environmental education, and research on green technologies. It also creates a National Fund for Environment and Sustainable Development and introduces eco-labeling and green taxation for high-pollution activities.', 'The Loi-cadre n° 99-12, promulgated in 2014, establishes Morocco’s national framework for environmental protection and sustainable development. It defines fundamental principles, objectives, and governance mechanisms for integrating sustainability into national policies. The law aims to:

Enhance environmental protection, biodiversity conservation, and pollution prevention.
