The law mandates territorial, social, and intergenerational solidarity principles and promotes public participation, environmental education, and research on green technologies. It also creates a National Fund for Environment and Sustainable Development and introduces eco-labeling and green taxation for high-pollution activities.', 'Morocco', 'climate', 'in_force', '2014-01-01'::date, 'Morocco', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/122_1', ARRAY['sdg2', 'sdg13', 'regulations', 'sdg7', 'mandatory', 'sdg16', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'morocco']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('f305ea2d-0c65-56d4-a9fc-e1d4f92c04b3', 'Investment in Mozambique Law No', 'Law on Investment in Mozambique Law No.3/93', 'Law No.3/93 is the investment law of Mozambique that was enacted in 1993. It provides the legal framework for investments in Mozambique, including foreign investments. The law guarantees the rights of investors and ensures the protection of their investments. It also establishes the conditions for the admission of foreign investments and regulates the procedures for the acquisition of assets and property by foreign investors. The law establishes the Mozambique Investment Promotion Centre (CPI), which is responsible for promoting and facilitating investments in the country. The CPI provides information to investors, assists with the establishment of new businesses, and provides support for the implementation of investment projects. This law requires companies to make certain disclosures as part of the investment process. Specifically, companies seeking investment permits must submit an investment proposal that includes information on the nature and scope of the investment, the proposed location, the amount of capital to be invested, and the estimated employment and production levels.', 'Law No.3/93 is the investment law of Mozambique that was enacted in 1993. It provides the legal framework for investments in Mozambique, including foreign investments. The law guarantees the rights of investors and ensures the protection of their investments. It also establishes the conditions for the admission of foreign investments and regulates the procedures for the acquisition of assets and property by foreign investors. The law establishes the Mozambique Investment Promotion Centre (CPI), which is responsible for promoting and facilitating investments in the country. The CPI provides information to investors, assists with the establishment of new businesses, and provides support for the implementation of investment projects. This law requires companies to make certain disclosures as part of the investment process. Specifically, companies seeking investment permits must submit an investment proposal that includes information on the nature and scope of the investment, the proposed location, the amount of capital to be invested, and the estimated employment and production levels.', 'Law No.3/93 is the investment law of Mozambique that was enacted in 1993. It provides the legal framework for investments in Mozambique, including foreign investments. The law guarantees the rights of investors and ensures the protection of their investments. It also establishes the conditions for the admission of foreign investments and regulates the procedures for the acquisition of assets and property by foreign investors. The law establishes the Mozambique Investment Promotion Centre (CPI), which is responsible for promoting and facilitating investments in the country. The CPI provides information to investors, assists with the establishment of new businesses, and provides support for the implementation of investment projects. This law requires companies to make certain disclosures as part of the investment process. Specifically, companies seeking investment permits must submit an investment proposal that includes information on the nature and scope of the investment, the proposed location, the amount of capital to be invested, and the estimated employment and production levels.', 'Mozambique', 'climate', 'in_force', '1993-01-01'::date, 'Mozambique', 'https://www.carrotsandsticks.org/policies/123_1', ARRAY['sdg8', 'regulations', 'mandatory', 'sdg12', 'disclosure', 'sdg15', 'mozambique']::text[]) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('96f6ba23-e4b6-5116-83d0-127a37e965aa', 'Myanmar Climate Change Policy', 'Myanmar Climate Change Policy', 'The Myanmar Climate Change Policy (MCCP), adopted in 2019, provides a strategic framework to address climate change adaptation and mitigation while ensuring sustainable development. It aligns with Myanmar’s Sustainable Development Plan (MSDP), the National Comprehensive Plan, and the Paris Agreement (2015).

Key policy objectives include:

Strengthening climate resilience through national, subnational, and local adaptation measures.
Mitigating greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions while transitioning to a low-carbon economy.
Integrating climate change considerations into sectoral policies, including energy, agriculture, forestry, and disaster risk management.
Enhancing public awareness and stakeholder participation in climate actions.
Promoting sustainable land use, natural resource management, and environmental conservation.
Ensuring financial and technological support for climate initiatives, particularly for vulnerable communities.
The policy highlights Myanmar’s vulnerability to extreme weather events (cyclones, floods, droughts) and the need for urgent climate action to protect livelihoods, ecosystems, and economic stability.', 'The Myanmar Climate Change Policy (MCCP), adopted in 2019, provides a strategic framework to address climate change adaptation and mitigation while ensuring sustainable development. It aligns with Myanmar’s Sustainable Development Plan (MSDP), the National Comprehensive Plan, and the Paris Agreement (2015).

