The policy highlights Myanmar’s vulnerability to extreme weather events (cyclones, floods, droughts) and the need for urgent climate action to protect livelihoods, ecosystems, and economic stability.', 'The Myanmar Climate Change Policy (MCCP), adopted in 2019, provides a strategic framework to address climate change adaptation and mitigation while ensuring sustainable development. It aligns with Myanmar’s Sustainable Development Plan (MSDP), the National Comprehensive Plan, and the Paris Agreement (2015).

