INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('590b2f42-10e4-58c6-9cc6-8499bfdda8fa', 'Myanmar Investment Law', 'Myanmar Investment Law', 'The Myanmar Investment Law, enacted in 2016, establishes a comprehensive legal framework for domestic and foreign investments in Myanmar. It aims to promote responsible investments while protecting investors’ rights and ensuring economic development. The law consolidates the Foreign Investment Law (2012) and the Myanmar Citizens Investment Law (2013) into a single investment framework.

Key provisions include:

Investor Protections: Guarantees against nationalization and expropriation, fair treatment for foreign and domestic investors, and dispute resolution mechanisms.
Investment Promotion & Incentives: Tax exemptions (up to 7 years for investments in less-developed zones), customs duty relief, and deductions for research & development.
Land Rights: Foreign investors can lease land for 50 years, with two 10-year extensions.
Sectoral Restrictions: Certain industries are reserved for local businesses or require government approval for foreign participation.
Environmental & Social Safeguards: Compliance with environmental conservation laws and mitigation of social impacts.
Investment Approvals: Large-scale and strategic projects require approval from the Myanmar Investment Commission (MIC).
The law seeks to attract foreign direct investment (FDI) while ensuring socioeconomic benefits for Myanmar citizens through job creation, infrastructure development, and technology transfer.', 'The Myanmar Investment Law, enacted in 2016, establishes a comprehensive legal framework for domestic and foreign investments in Myanmar. It aims to promote responsible investments while protecting investors’ rights and ensuring economic development. The law consolidates the Foreign Investment Law (2012) and the Myanmar Citizens Investment Law (2013) into a single investment framework.

