INSERT INTO regulations (id, title, formal_title, summary, description, full_description, region, category, status, effective_date, source_name, source_url, tags) VALUES ('7179e445-89fe-5c66-9df8-569f7a20d32a', 'Myanmar Environmental Conservation Law (Pyidaungsu Hluttaw Law', 'Environmental Conservation Law (Pyidaungsu Hluttaw Law No. 9', 'The Environmental Conservation Law (ECL), enacted in 2012, establishes Myanmar’s legal framework for environmental protection, pollution control, and natural resource conservation. The law aims to balance economic development with sustainability by setting environmental standards, regulatory measures, and enforcement mechanisms.

Key provisions include:

Environmental Quality Standards: The government sets air, water, noise, and waste management standards (Ch. VI).
Pollution Control: Businesses must comply with waste disposal and emissions regulations (Ch. VII).
Environmental Impact Assessments (EIA & SIA): Mandates assessments before launching projects with significant environmental impact (Ch. VII, Sec. 14-16).
Land Use & Resource Conservation: Regulates forest, water, and mineral resource management (Ch. IX).
Environmental Emergency Response: Establishes protocols for addressing environmental disasters (Ch. V).
Regulatory Enforcement: Businesses violating environmental regulations face fines, penalties, or suspension (Ch. XII-XIII).
The law promotes sustainable development, corporate environmental responsibility, and regulatory transparency while aligning Myanmar with international environmental agreements.', 'The Environmental Conservation Law (ECL), enacted in 2012, establishes Myanmar’s legal framework for environmental protection, pollution control, and natural resource conservation. The law aims to balance economic development with sustainability by setting environmental standards, regulatory measures, and enforcement mechanisms.

Key provisions include:

Environmental Quality Standards: The government sets air, water, noise, and waste management standards (Ch. VI).
Pollution Control: Businesses must comply with waste disposal and emissions regulations (Ch. VII).
